IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, sections 2 and 2.1: the special qualifying factor, the specially qualified individual,
-- and which pension amount the Act means when it says "the amount of a full monthly pension" and
-- "the pensioner's monthly pension".

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "specially qualified individual means a person who has not resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years
-- of age for an aggregate period of ten or more years other than such a person to whom a pension or allowance
-- was payable (a) for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month, or (b) for the month of January 2001 or an
-- earlier month, where, before March 7, 1996, the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a
-- permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act"
--
-- The definition gives no day at which the ten years are counted. The special qualifying factor counts the
-- aggregate "as of the last day of the immediately preceding month", and the same figure is used here (fork F4
-- in NOTES.md). The aggregate period is a number of years, a fraction of a year being a fraction.
DECLARE `Special qualification facts` HAS
    `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS A NUMBER
    `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:78 | specially qualified individual means a person who has not resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age for an aggregate period of ten or more years other than such a person to whom a pension or allowance was payable
-- src:79 | (a) for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month, or
-- src:80 | (b) for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month, where, before March 7, 1996, the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act; (particulier déterminé)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "specially qualified individual" (src:78-80)
GIVEN facts IS A `Special qualification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a specially qualified individual` facts MEANS
        facts's `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` LESS THAN 10
    AND (NOT (  facts's `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month`
             OR (    facts's `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month`
                 AND facts's `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident`)))

-- "special qualifying factor of a person for a month before April 1996 means one and for a month after
-- March 1996 means (a) one, where the person is not a specially qualified individual, and (b) where the person
-- is a specially qualified individual, the fraction of which (i) the numerator is the aggregate period
-- (expressed in the number of years and, where the number of years is not a whole number, rounded down to the
-- next lower whole number) as of the last day of the immediately preceding month, during which the individual
-- has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, and (ii) the denominator is 10"
--
-- The month is any date in the month. "A fraction" is a fraction of one (0.3 for three years of ten).
-- src:73 | special qualifying factor of a person for a month before April 1996 means one and for a month after March 1996 means
-- src:74 | (a) one, where the person is not a specially qualified individual, and
-- src:75 | (b) where the person is a specially qualified individual, the fraction of which
-- src:76 | (i) the numerator is the aggregate period (expressed in the number of years and, where the number of years is not a whole number, rounded down to the next lower whole number) as of the last day of the immediately preceding month, during which the individual has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, and
-- src:77 | (ii) the denominator is 10; (facteur d’admissibilité)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "special qualifying factor" (src:73-77)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Special qualification facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month facts MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- for a month before April 1996 means one
        IF `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN (YearMonthDay 1996 4 1)
        THEN 1
        -- (a) one, where the person is not a specially qualified individual
        IF NOT `the person is a specially qualified individual` facts
        THEN 1
        -- (b) the fraction whose numerator is the whole years of residence and whose denominator is 10
        OTHERWISE
            (FLOOR (facts's `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month`)) DIVIDED BY 10

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Section 2.1. Three amounts of pension are in play in Parts I to III, and the Act says in terms which one
-- these phrases mean (the table in NOTES.md, "Instructions to the pieces", lists the three):
--   (1) a reference to "the amount of a full monthly pension" means the amount "as it is calculated in
--       accordance with section 7, that has not been increased under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)";
--   (2) "pensioner's monthly pension" in subsections 12(5) and 22(2), and "pension" in subsection 12(5.1), mean
--       a pension "that has not been increased under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)".
-- Each rule below is given the amount before and the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)
-- (the same amount when nothing was deferred) and answers with the amount before, so that the exclusion is
-- written down in one named place and a test shows that the increased amount makes no difference.
-- The amounts themselves are worked out by piece oa1 (sections 3(3), 7 and 7.1).
-- src:86 | Amount of full monthly pension
-- src:87 | 2.1 (1) In this Act, a reference to the amount of a full monthly pension means the amount of a full monthly pension, as it is calculated in accordance with section 7, that has not been increased under subsection 7.1(1) or (2).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2.1(1) (src:86-87)
GIVEN `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a full monthly pension` `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the amount after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` MEANS
    `the amount calculated in accordance with section 7, before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`

-- src:88 | Monthly pension
-- src:89 | (2) The terms pensioner’s monthly pension in subsections 12(5) and 22(2) and pension in subsection 12(5.1) mean, respectively, a pensioner’s monthly pension and a pension that have not been increased under subsection 7.1(1) or (2).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2.1(2), "pensioner's monthly pension" in subsections 12(5) and 22(2) (src:88-89)
GIVEN `the pensioner's monthly pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the pensioner's monthly pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pensioner's monthly pension in subsections 12(5) and 22(2)` `the pensioner's monthly pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the pensioner's monthly pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` MEANS
    `the pensioner's monthly pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2.1(2), "pension" in subsection 12(5.1) (src:88-89)
GIVEN `the pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pension in subsection 12(5.1)` `the pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` `the pension after any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)` MEANS
    `the pension before any increase under subsection 7.1(1) or (2)`
